      "id": "oom-context-error-check",
      "change_ids": [
        "g0003"
      ],
      "kind": "check",
      "necessary": true,
      "established": true,
      "requirement": "Update the existing XInclude malloc-failure check to use the error channel that the changed memory-error helper actually sets.",
      "target_route": "Supply a well-formed document with an xi:include and set the encoded allocation limit to the ordinal of xmlXIncludeNewRef's allocation, after parsing and context creation. The fuzzer's one-shot failure reaches xmlXIncludeErrMemory; processing then reports no fallback before the harness checks xmlXIncludeGetLastError.",
      "failure_condition": "fuzzAllocFailed is true, while the XInclude context's errNo is not XML_ERR_NO_MEMORY, so the existing xmlFuzzCheckMallocFailure aborts.",
      "alternative_paths": "The helper sets the global error, but the existing check reads the XInclude context. The later no-fallback error can set errNo to a different code; no target call reconciles these values.",
      "source_evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-b954120108bc446b7b7b",
